WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.200
Hi, everyone.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.679
My name is Sean Spitzer, senior instructor for Epic Games.

3
00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:08.880
Today, we're going to look at an overview for Perforce

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.480
and ICVFX and how those two work together

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.300
in a virtual production environment.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.000
So let's get started.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.359
What I want to point out is when working with Unreal,

8
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:21.160
you want to make sure initially,

9
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.600
like you saw Kevin run you through a few things,

10
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.160
you want to make sure that you know your server,

11
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.920
your username, and you also want

12
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.879
to make sure you're connected to the right workspace.

13
00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:34.920
These are very important when working with Unreal.

14
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.039
And if we go to the Unreal Engine momentarily,

15
00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:42.789
I can show you exactly where those settings can be found.

16
00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:44.810
If you look at the bottom right corner here,

17
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.729
you will see that we are connected to source control.

18
00:00:47.729 --> 00:00:49.689
I can click on this icon, and you'll

19
00:00:49.689 --> 00:00:52.950
see that we have View Change List, Submit Content,

20
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.329
and Change Source Control Settings.

21
00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:58.130
Now, that little menu you saw in my slide deck,

22
00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.170
you'll actually see it here.

23
00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.770
This will show me that I'm choosing Perforce,

24
00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.590
but I can also choose any other version

25
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.920
control of my choosing.

26
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.040
So we're working with Perforce,

27
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.120
and one of the key things you want to make sure

28
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.400
that you are connected to is one, of course, your server,

29
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.900
but also you want to make sure your username

30
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.159
and your workspace are lined up correctly,

31
00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:21.700
and you're able to find the available workspaces

32
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.140
within that session.

33
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.510
So let's go back to the slides.

34
00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:29.670
You'll see also that we have other options that will pop up,

35
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.109
and this depends on your workflow

36
00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:34.230
and where you're at when you're editing.

37
00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.689
And what I mean by that, you'll

38
00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:40.469
see in this particular menu in blue in that yellow box

39
00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:43.510
that we have in our slide deck, the one on the left,

40
00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.769
you'll notice it says Connect to Source Control.

41
00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:48.430
For obvious reasons, that's because we are not.

42
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.069
And you'll see some of these change, again, like I said,

43
00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.909
conditionally based on what you are doing

44
00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:56.750
and your activity within Unreal.

45
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.790
You'll also see once you make changes,

46
00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:02.670
you will see a persistent session changes show up,

47
00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.560
as well as submit content as you're making changes.

48
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.020
Towards the bottom, you can also

49
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.860
go into Unreal within your content browser,

50
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.939
and you can also check out assets.

51
00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:16.180
Let's go to Unreal just for a moment,

52
00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.509
and I can show you how that works.

53
00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:23.689
So say we made a change over here to one of our NDCs.

54
00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:25.849
I can right click at any time and see

55
00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:29.409
that this object in my overall session

56
00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:31.250
is connected to source control.

57
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.610
I can check it out, I can refresh,

58
00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.409
I can check my history, and check the differences

59
00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:38.419
against the depot.

60
00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:40.919
All those things are at our fingertips.

61
00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:43.680
Let's go back to the slides for a moment.

62
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.159
So the order of operations I want to point out

63
00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:49.080
is check out your modified files, number one.

64
00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.680
Number two, turn on persistent session changes.

65
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.150
And three, then you'll submit.

66
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.110
So you want to verify your server,

67
00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.830
your workspace, and your stream.

68
00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.750
That is key up front.

69
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.990
But then, like I said before, the order

70
00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.789
of operations for submitting is

71
00:03:04.789 --> 00:03:06.550
to check out your modified files,

72
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.710
turn on your persistent session changes,

73
00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.069
and then submit your file changes.

74
00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:14.270
So let me go down to the next slide here,

75
00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.030
and we'll see that we also want

76
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.669
to make sure that in Switchboard

77
00:03:17.669 --> 00:03:19.550
that we're going in the right direction when

78
00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.490
it comes to our directories.

79
00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.009
And we want to make sure that we're talking

80
00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:24.770
to Unreal correctly.

81
00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.050
So let's go to Unreal for a moment.

82
00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:30.419
You'll see that we have our Switchboard open.

83
00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:33.340
With our Switchboard open, we can go in here

84
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.060
and now check such things as our change list here,

85
00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.159
and line this up with what we have in Perforce.

86
00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:42.860
You also can check things within your settings

87
00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.939
in making sure that Perforce

88
00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:47.780
and your source control is active,

89
00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:48.699
making sure that you're going

90
00:03:48.699 --> 00:03:51.139
to the right engine version and path.

91
00:03:51.139 --> 00:03:55.180
And you'll see here that we are connected to 5.1.

92
00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.919
All these things need to be considered

93
00:03:56.919 --> 00:03:59.099
when working with Unreal to make things flow

94
00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:02.020
a lot better for you when working with Perforce.

95
00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:02.860
So let me go ahead,

96
00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.300
and I'm going to open up Perforce here for a moment,

97
00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.819
and point out a few things when it comes

98
00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:08.759
to working with Perforce.

99
00:04:08.759 --> 00:04:11.919
You don't always have to set things in through Switchboard.

100
00:04:11.919 --> 00:04:14.099
If you initially just want to check your files,

101
00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:16.639
you can do that within Perforce by itself.

102
00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:18.800
So don't think that you have to launch everything

103
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.319
within Switchboard to be able to get to Perforce.

104
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.079
You can isolate and work in Perforce first,

105
00:04:24.079 --> 00:04:26.800
and then eventually go in and send things

106
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.139
over to Switchboard, and then send them to your wall.

107
00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:32.839
All that can be done according to your needs,

108
00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.680
and if you just need to check something

109
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.139
that maybe the VAD department has sent to you,

110
00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:39.040
and you want to make sure before you go to the wall

111
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.439
and commit with Switchboard

112
00:04:40.439 --> 00:04:41.879
that everything's in the right spot.

113
00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:43.579
So you're more than welcome to do so.

114
00:04:43.579 --> 00:04:45.579
And you can do so simply by right-clicking

115
00:04:45.579 --> 00:04:46.899
and opening up that file,

116
00:04:46.899 --> 00:04:49.319
or double-clicking it in Perforce.

117
00:04:49.319 --> 00:04:51.439
Your depot stream, like mentioned before,

118
00:04:51.439 --> 00:04:53.920
is very important that you know you're pulling things

119
00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.480
from the correct stream.

120
00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.000
You don't want to forget about this.

121
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.839
In our workspace, if I needed to find my check,

122
00:05:00.839 --> 00:05:04.439
my change list, I would not necessarily go

123
00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:07.199
to our actual project, but I'd go to the top

124
00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:09.199
of the folder that's housing

125
00:05:09.199 --> 00:05:11.199
all of our project information.

126
00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:15.279
And that's where your change list information is going to be.

127
00:05:15.279 --> 00:05:18.319
So I can check right over here with history viewed,

128
00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:19.759
and you can also go to Windows

129
00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:23.839
to get to those particular views.

130
00:05:23.839 --> 00:05:26.519
And in history, I can choose my change list

131
00:05:26.519 --> 00:05:29.040
and find which one that I'm working with,

132
00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.620
and I can compare that if I'm running into trouble

133
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.279
within Switchboard and noticing

134
00:05:33.279 --> 00:05:35.680
that things aren't quite syncing.

135
00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.699
Whenever you're adding things to the depot,

136
00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:39.939
make sure that you select all the files

137
00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.680
within your Perforce.

138
00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.199
And what I mean by that is say I needed

139
00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:46.800
to add all of these into Perforce.

140
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.560
I'm going to shift select all the files,

141
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.240
but I also want to make sure that these sub folders

142
00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.079
are open when I'm selecting

143
00:05:54.079 --> 00:05:56.519
and make sure all the content is selected.

144
00:05:56.519 --> 00:05:59.399
If you just select them and you'll notice

145
00:05:59.399 --> 00:06:01.459
that there's some files being skipped over,

146
00:06:01.459 --> 00:06:03.680
even though we selected the parent folder.

147
00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.040
So you want to make sure you get everything

148
00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:05.899
in the hierarchy.

149
00:06:05.899 --> 00:06:07.920
So open these up, select them,

150
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.480
and you should be on the right path

151
00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.639
to being able to mark them for add

152
00:06:11.639 --> 00:06:14.160
and then submitting them.

153
00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.800
Whenever you're running into trouble

154
00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:17.959
and Perforce has given you a little bit of issues

155
00:06:17.959 --> 00:06:20.339
and you can't seem to get all the information

156
00:06:20.339 --> 00:06:23.319
to sync correctly, you can at times go in here,

157
00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:24.879
not just get latest version,

158
00:06:24.879 --> 00:06:26.899
but you can actually get a revision.

159
00:06:26.899 --> 00:06:28.519
And when you open up revision,

160
00:06:28.519 --> 00:06:30.279
you can tell it to force operation

161
00:06:30.279 --> 00:06:32.139
and to load all the files in there

162
00:06:32.139 --> 00:06:34.420
if you suspect that things aren't quite syncing

163
00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.579
or talking to each other like they should.

164
00:06:36.579 --> 00:06:39.639
Now, no software is perfect, including Perforce.

165
00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:41.680
And then sometimes Perforce and Switchboard

166
00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.519
may have some issues

167
00:06:42.519 --> 00:06:44.199
where they're not quite talking to each other,

168
00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:45.920
but this will put you on the right path

169
00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.180
if you need to make sure that Perforce is loaded,

170
00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.839
all your files are in the right spot,

171
00:06:49.839 --> 00:06:51.839
and then you can work a little bit cleanly

172
00:06:51.839 --> 00:06:53.680
and a little bit with a clear conscience

173
00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.040
knowing that Switchboard is getting the updated data.

174
00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.759
So let's go back to the slides.

175
00:06:59.759 --> 00:07:03.079
We now see that we also have different ways

176
00:07:03.079 --> 00:07:05.279
in which you can tackle Perforce.

177
00:07:05.279 --> 00:07:07.160
And we talked about how you can check

178
00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.839
and triple check the issues that you may run into.

179
00:07:09.839 --> 00:07:12.319
And again, it is very crucial, you'll see it here,

180
00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:14.160
that you're on the right string.

181
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.759
Like I mentioned before.

182
00:07:15.759 --> 00:07:18.240
If you're not, you're going to find out quickly

183
00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.980
how things are not gonna sync,

184
00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.240
as well as Unreal will not give you the correct data.

185
00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.079
And you may see,

186
00:07:24.079 --> 00:07:26.480
hey, I partially have some files that are working

187
00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:29.480
and some aren't because your files aren't lined up

188
00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.060
with what you had previously.

189
00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.139
So it's always good to triple check that.

190
00:07:34.139 --> 00:07:37.420
You'll notice also that you have Game Sync

191
00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:38.779
at your fingertips,

192
00:07:38.779 --> 00:07:41.399
and we offer that for you to be able to use it.

193
00:07:41.399 --> 00:07:46.399
Now is Game Sync a one all be all perfect system

194
00:07:47.259 --> 00:07:49.240
in which it fixes all your problems?

195
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.839
No, it actually is just a shell for Perforce.

196
00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:55.579
It makes things cleaner, it makes things smoother,

197
00:07:55.579 --> 00:07:58.560
but it doesn't necessarily make Perforce work better

198
00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.160
or necessarily make Switchboard magically

199
00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.720
become even more robust and do different

200
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:09.560
or new or complete things the way that you want.

201
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.839
So Game Sync, again, is just a shell.

202
00:08:12.839 --> 00:08:14.680
You can use it, it works great.

203
00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.120
I've used it before.

204
00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.720
It's a nice and clean interface,

205
00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.019
but it really is just a shell interface

206
00:08:20.019 --> 00:08:21.680
to be able to get Perforce

207
00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.500
to sync a bit better with Unreal,

208
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.000
but it doesn't do anything new.

209
00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.519
You can actually live without it,

210
00:08:28.519 --> 00:08:30.399
but it is kind of cool to have

211
00:08:30.399 --> 00:08:33.840
because it helps you a little bit navigating your system.
